WEBVTT

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:04.520
And so, let's all have a listen.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.270
Dear Hell...

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:14.570
Jigoku mitai ni asobitai
I want to have a good time like Hell

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:19.700
Jigoku mitai ni yasumitai
I want to rest like Hell

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.540
Jigoku mitai na nidoneshite
I want to go back to sleep like Hell

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:29.130
Teiji de agaritai
And finish work on time

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:34.970
Jigoku mitai ni tabesugite
I ate too much like Hell

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:39.720
Jigoku mitai ni nomisugita
I drank too much like Hell

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:44.980
Aa sonna wake de
Ah, for these reasons

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:50.230
Jigoku mitai
It's like Hell

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.650
Sonna toki koso deban desu
At such a time it's all the more his turn on stage

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:55.320
Hoozuki-sama ga moriageru
Mr. Hozuki livens things up

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:57.410
Omakase kudasai!
Please leave it to me!

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:03.000
Aa jigoku jigoku mainichi jigoku
Ah, Hell, Hell, every day Hell

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.580
Jigoku jigoku
Hell, Hell

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:08.250
"Uso desho?!"
"You can't mean that, right?!"

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:13.170
Jigoku jigoku youkoso jigoku
Hell, Hell, welcome to Hell

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:14.010
Atchi muite
Look that way

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:14.590
Kotchi muite
Look this way

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:15.720
Abikyoukan!
Pandemonium!

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:17.090
Gongo! Doudan!
What the hell!

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:18.890
Shitsureishimashita!
Pardon me!

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:23.890
Sonna kanji no
In that kind of way

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:27.980
A! Jigoku desu! Jajajajan!
Ah! It's Hell! Ta ta ta-da!

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:28.980
Katsu!
Curses!

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:36.280
HELL
NEWSPAPER

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:38.490
Momotaro, Momotaro...

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:42.240
those millet dumplings you carry around your waist...

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:47.330
HELL
NEWSPAPER

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:45.750
Computer viruses and cybercrime...
Give me one of them, please.

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:47.540
Things are tough in the Mundane World, too.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.040
The Muromachi Era, when I was born,
was also pretty tough.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:54.420
Bad demons would come
and diseases would run rampant...

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:56.800
Ah, diseases, huh?

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:00.600
Different eras have different sets of problems.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:01.800
Excuse me!

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:04.720
Ah, it's the police. I wonder what's the matter.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:10.230
Momotaro is one of your acquaintances,
Mr. Hozuki, correct?

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:12.730
Yes.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:17.950
There's something I'd like his cooperation with
regarding an incident on Ogre Island...

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:19.030
Oh?

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:19.820
Huh?
Oh?

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:27.120
Onki

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:30.120
Full Moon
Paradise
Bunny
Chinese
Medicine

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:34.590
Hey.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:40.800
Thank you for your call. You have reached
Bunny Chinese Medicine: Full Moon Para...

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:43.010
Oh, it's YOU again.

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:44.100
Huh?

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:47.020
Tao-taro, phone's for you.

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:48.730
For me?

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:53.820
I'm here now.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:56.030
Uh-huh...

00:02:57.190 --> 00:02:59.780
Uh-huh... Uh-huh...

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.530
What? "Ogre Island"?

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:18.420
THIS IS COSPLAY
MOMOTARO

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:18.420
ENTHUSIAST

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:18.420
Uh... so what is this?

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:21.550
At this point, I find this kinda thing embarrassing.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:23.550
I thought it would lift up your spirits...

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:25.510
Wow!
Whoa, it brings back memories seeing you like this!

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:26.560
Whoa, it brings back memories seeing you like this!

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:29.020
We will be heading to the Mundane World now.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:30.100
"The Mundane World"?

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.020
W-w-wait just a minute, please!

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:34.190
What? What now? What's the meaning of this?

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:37.570
I was only told I'd be cooperating
in an investigation related to Ogre Island...

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:38.780
Special Passage Permit

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:42.240
I'll explain on the way there.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:46.700
DEMON

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:48.660
In Japanese, "demon" is derived from "conceal."
It means that which cannot be seen.

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:47.410
CONCEAL
DEMON

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:48.290
DEMON

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:54.460
That is to say, it refers to the whole of frightening,
unidentifiable things in the Mundane World.

00:03:55.880 --> 00:04:00.970
THE
FIRST DAY
OF SPRING

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:58.300
The demons of the lunar calendar's last day of winter are,

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:00.880
rather than monsters, thought of
as evil gods of pestilence.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:05.300
These gods of pestilence
are also known by the name "Onki."

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:10.770
In the past, many of the demons who ran wild
in the Mundane Word were such Onki.

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:15.150
They are by nature a type of demon native to Hell,

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:20.070
but some of ruffians among them took up residence
in the Mundane World, where they rage about.

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:26.530
Shiro, earlier you said, "Bad demons would come
and diseases would run rampant," did you not?

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:27.450
Hm?

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:27.740
Hm?
Hm?

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:30.290
Momotaro's ogres may also be Onki.

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:36.210
Anyway, that Ogre Island, where the ogres used to live,
is apparently once again home to ogres.

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:38.920
If they're Onki, further investigation is required.

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:42.340
To the humans of that era,

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:42.470
Influenza

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:46.340
they were known for having a talent for spreading
the most troubling types of epidemics.
Tuberculosis... Influenza...

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:43.630
Tuberculosis

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:45.050
Influenza

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:45.510
Tuberculosis

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:53.270
Their ravaging of the Mundane World despite not
originally being from there runs afoul of Hell law.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:53.730
Yokai Originally from the Mundane World
ONKI
Whatever they did in the Mundane World
in the past is of no concern

00:04:54.730 --> 00:05:00.150
Currently, whether Ogre Island is inhabited
by ogres from those days or by Onki...

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:04.360
is something I would like Momotaro to confirm.

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:07.660
Ah, that's what this is about.

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:11.990
So then, why am I being accompanied by you,
Hozuki, and not the police?

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:14.620
If they end up being Onki
who're not doing much of anything,

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:17.000
I'd like them to work at the Disease Suffering Realm...

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:21.880
I've also told the police I'll report immediately
if anything comes up.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:27.220
Well, there haven't been any accounts of
extensive damage, so I'm not even sure if they're there...

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:31.720
Even if there are some, it's possible they're just
quietly living there, you know?

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:35.770
Indeed. There's also the possibility they're simply
humans who look somewhat ogre-like.

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:41.150
Ah, like one of those hermits there's occasionally
a feature story about on TV...

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:43.860
That's actually something I'd like to see.

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:47.280
Hey, starting with this outfit of mine,

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:50.280
you're just involving yourself in this
for the entertainment of it, aren't you?

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:52.490
Infectious diseases, huh?

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:57.790
You know, despite that Momotaro was healthy
as could be back then... stupidly so.

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:01.750
Peaches drive away wickedness.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:05.170
The Heaven-sent peach child should
be immune to infectious diseases.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:10.850
I can see it.

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:20.440
KEEP OUT
DANGEROUS
SHORE BREAK

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:26.650
Oh... This is it! This is the island!

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:29.360
Seeing it now, that's quite clear.

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:36.080
It's so clear that apparently the local people see it
as the epitome of an "Ogre Island-looking place."

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:37.660
I totally get it!

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:50.970
This takes me back...
I'm actually feeling kinda nervous now.

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:53.510
You want me to open the lock again?!

00:06:57.270 --> 00:06:59.940
Well, seems it was unlocked.

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:02.900
Feels kind of like a countryside residence?

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:09.150
Somehow... it feels like a strangely modern living space...

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:12.280
Was it like this the last time we came?

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:16.740
No, long ago it was regular old bare cave.

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:18.500
You're right...

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:23.210
But the overall taste this place exhibits means
the inhabitants probably aren't human, you know?

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:28.170
In any event, they sure have renovated
this place into a modern cave...

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:32.130
So, when are you gonna make a serious effort, then?!

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:36.010
You've already been saying, "I'll make an effort!
I'll make an effort" for 200 years now!

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:38.600
When are you gonna give your mom a grandchild?!

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:40.430
SHUT UP, YOU OLD HAG!

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:43.270
Angel Olive is the only waifu for me!

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:47.980
So when is that Olive girl gonna come out
through the screen and introduce herself to me?!

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:49.280
SHUT UP ALREADY!

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:52.610
You're an Onki and yet all you do
is play around on that computer!

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:56.410
Don't you ever get the urge
to snatch a human treasure or two?!

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:58.910
What the heck is a "treasure" nowadays?!

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:01.830
Don't make light of the security systems
of the modern human race!

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:05.130
Right now the Onki are in a weaker position, you know!

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:09.050
Well, then as an Onki go
and spread at least one disease!

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:11.630
Hey, as his father, come here and say something!

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:16.470
Hayaru! Listen here...
When your mother and I fought with Momotaro-

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:18.600
In the end, you lost, didn't you?

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:23.310
Ogre Island Jr. is a total shut-in...

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:28.690
Yipes... That father is undoubtedly
the ogre from back then...

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:31.070
Your mother is getting on in years, you know!

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:34.860
Even stealing vegetables from the fields
by the opposing shore is tiring for me!

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:38.530
And for your dad, just spreading around
the common cold is about all...

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:41.830
The future of epidemics is resting on your shoulders!

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:45.920
There's no way we're mistaken
about these being Onki, right?

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:50.880
Back in your day, they also did some stealing
while they were out spreading diseases, didn't they?

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:54.470
Yeah, but what these ones are doing
is awfully small potatoes...

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:56.340
We're talking the common cold...

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:58.470
Minor as it may be, it's still unlawful.

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:01.220
Those parents need to be questioned by the police.

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:06.230
But it seems like Hayaru
has zero interest in spreading anything.

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:10.110
Ah, sorry!

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:12.150
What are you doing, you idiot?!

00:09:13.030 --> 00:09:13.780
Who're you?!

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:16.660
M-Momotaro?!

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:20.910
I can't believe it! You've been living
in the Mundane World this whole time?!

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:24.830
No, I'm dead, alright...

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:28.080
So then, you've come to defeat our son, have you?!

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:29.170
What?!

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:30.710
Hayaru, stay in your room!

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:32.800
I won't let you anywhere near Hayaru!

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:36.720
Hey, didn't you just lecture your son about
how he should become independent?!

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:42.060
In the end, isn't it the way you try to protect him
from everything like that the problem here?

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:45.520
Momotaro shared an adult opinion with the ogres!

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:48.400
BEST
IN
JAPAN

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:48.520
Amazing! The old you almost seems hard to believe!

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:52.820
I pity... your son.

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:54.900
How dare you suddenly show up here and admonish us!

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:57.070
You're the one who least knows
what's best for him, alright?!

00:09:57.400 --> 00:10:00.570
We didn't actually come here to defeat you.

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:04.330
We're just cooperating with an investigation
by the Crow-Tengu Police.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:06.080
"P-police," you say?!

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:07.870
I won't let you arrest our son!

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:10.630
No, not your son... it's you they're after!

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:14.340
In the first place, your son hasn't done anything at all...
neither good nor bad!

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:15.970
Hey, you there!

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:17.220
Who's this guy?!

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:18.220
Always messing around on your computer...

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:20.050
Ah, hey, stop! Stop that, please!
Always messing around on your computer...

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:21.010
Ah, hey, stop! Stop that, please!
did cause you to draw a bit of attention,
so I'm going to investigate.

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:22.850
Ah... umm... uhh...
did cause you to draw a bit of attention,
so I'm going to investigate.

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:25.850
Hold on! Just what are you planning
to do to our Hayaru?!

00:10:25.850 --> 00:10:27.140
Ah, wai...!

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:27.850
Wai...!

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:31.980
Hm?

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:36.530
Your son's the one who should be
taken into custody first, isn't he?

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:40.110
This computer is being used
to create and distribute viruses.

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:43.280
"Viruses"?!

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:46.370
No way... did you...?!

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:50.670
I had actually planned to tell you
on your birthday, Mom...

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:52.040
Hayaru!

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:55.000
Oh, my, that's quite impressive of you!

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:56.460
You've moved your father so much that I'm crying now.

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:59.010
Viruses... They deal in those kind of epidemics, too?
You've moved your father so much that I'm crying now.

00:10:59.010 --> 00:10:59.880
Viruses... They deal in those kind of epidemics, too?
Sorry I said I never should've given birth to you!

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:02.140
Hello, Yoshitsune.
Sorry I said I never should've given birth to you!

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:05.220
Full Moon
Paradise
Bunny
Chinese

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:05.220
Medicine

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:08.680
Tao-taro, a letter of appreciation, huh? That's fantastic!

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:06.220
YOSHITSUNE
CROW-TENGU POLICE

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:06.220
MR. MOMOTARO
LETTER OF
APPRECIATION

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:12.350
What are you feeling so down about?

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:18.740
Well... To think the ogres I defeated ended up like that...

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:33.830
BEYOND THIS POINT:
THE OFFICES
OF SHOKO

00:11:46.970 --> 00:11:47.770
Huh...?

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:49.810
Is this guy here alive?

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:53.730
He's dead. You and I are both also dead.

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:58.820
Well, in the sense that he seems lifeless,
I can see what made you want to ask that.

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:07.910
Animals Don't Forget One's Kindness

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:13.040
Walks are simply the very best activity,
you know?! I love 'em!

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:16.130
Hey, did you come just expecting to take a walk?

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:17.590
Huh?! That's not what we're doing?!

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:22.970
Mr. Hozuki, why bother to take me along
for your trip to the Offices of Shoko?

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:26.640
After all, it's usually only Shiro
who accompanies you on these trips.

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:33.190
For quite some time now, King Shoko
has been telling me to bring you all along with me.

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:36.730
King Shoko must be a huge animal lover, huh?

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:38.400
You seriously think that's the reason?

00:12:38.820 --> 00:12:42.740
What would you do? If the Offices of Shoko
are actually an animal kingdom, I mean.

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:45.780
Hm?

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:48.740
Bingo!

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:51.830
Second Judgement:
Offices of Shoko

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:13.310
There's a full-cheeked old guy here who seems
to have abilities even beyond those of Snow White!

00:13:13.310 --> 00:13:15.980
Wow, this guy's a real rare-animal nut.

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:17.230
An okapi,

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:18.730
a pygmy hippo,

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:20.730
an Iriomote cat,

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:23.360
an Okinawa rail, a kiwi,

00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:25.400
as well as...

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:27.280
AAH! A KAKAPO!

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:30.240
King Shoko, you've now taken in a kakapo
as one or your subordinates?!

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:34.250
That's right, a kakapo. Cute, isn't it?

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:38.170
I've heard of kakapos...

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:40.540
They're those flightless birds from New Zealand.

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:44.380
I have more foxes now, too. This is a fennec fox.

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:47.090
Whoa... so that's a fox.

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:48.800
It's so small...

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:52.100
Here's a Tibetan sand fox!

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:53.560
A TIBET SAND!

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:58.230
Mr. Hozuki, you care about this species of animal
so much you've got an abbreviation for it?!

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:02.270
It hasn't been that long since it was discovered
in the Mundane World, you know!

00:14:02.270 --> 00:14:03.730
O-oh...

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:05.610
What kind of Offices are these anyway?!

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:09.620
These kind of Offices.

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:10.280
Kiwi

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:11.330
Okinawa Rail

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:12.660
Iriomote Cat
Okinawa Rail

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:25.300
I think I get the general idea.

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:29.390
Probably, King Shoko just wanted
to get a look at us, you know?

00:14:29.390 --> 00:14:30.800
Yeah, you're right.

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:35.720
Mr. Hozuki, why didn't you become
the chief of staff here?

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:39.270
Well, at the beginning this place wasn't like this.

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:45.900
I originally lived in an enchanted land
alongside deer and birds.

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:49.860
So, just like that, I took on animals as subordinates.

00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:52.910
From then on, they just kept on increasing in number...

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:57.290
And eventually animals came to make up
the bulk of Hell minions here.

00:14:57.660 --> 00:15:03.540
Upon seeing that, I admired,
"Ah, so it's okay to do this kind of thing."

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:06.340
King Shoko set the precedent,

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:11.720
so no one was able to stop Mr. Hozuki's plan
to bolster the ranks of Hell minion animals, huh?!

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:18.890
And, this here is his chief of staff.

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:19.810
The most peculiar animal in the whole world!

00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:20.440
Hi.
The most peculiar animal in the whole world!

00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:21.150
The most peculiar animal in the whole world!

00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:22.650
Strangely enough, I can believe it!

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:26.780
King Shoko, ever since back
when he was in the enchanted land,

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:30.990
was so friendly with animals that they
would often come stop by his house.

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:33.200
Note: A short story in which a cellist gains instight into music through
interacting with anthropomorphized animals.
Like "Gauche the Cellist," huh?

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:33.570
Note: A short story in which a cellist gains instight into music through
interacting with anthropomorphized animals.

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:38.410
It's true that King Shoko seems approachable
since he doesn't display the least bit of hostility!

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:42.670
Which is why he gets surrounded by animals
when he heads to the forest.

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:45.380
Not too much different from right now, huh?

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:51.970
During the Sino-Japanese Goodwill Games
some 1,000 years ago, the panda got headhunted.

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:56.050
He placed highly in both sorcery and intellectual testing.

00:15:56.050 --> 00:15:58.310
Which is why I asked him to please join me.

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:01.640
King Shoko is great at diplomacy, you see.

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:03.940
Really? Didn't expect that.

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:07.110
The panda shows up places wearing a hat like this!

00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:09.740
No way there could be a country
that's not delighted by that!

00:16:09.940 --> 00:16:10.860
True!

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:14.110
The year-end gifts are straight out of a fairy tale!

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:17.660
Harmony! Don't the dead who come here
end up feeling comforted?!

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:21.460
No, this is the second of the Offices of the Ten Kings.

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:22.870
It's not a lenient place.

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:29.760
Often, people say that when you die,
a former pet you once had will come to greet you.

00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:36.300
This is the place that happens.
Pets are called in as material witnesses.

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:37.550
That's a tough reunion!

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:39.720
Wouldn't want to meet again for that kinda reason!

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:43.390
Apparently, it's possible to see
a seriously unexpected side of people.

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:46.770
Mikke

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:49.650
For example, how a scary-looking guy is actually
super sweet, or how a friendly guy treats his pets coldly.
Mikke buddy, Mikke buddy, what's the matter?! You tired meow?

00:16:49.940 --> 00:16:52.860
Now that's embarrassing... in either case.

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:58.370
Well, I can see how they'd indeed be the best witnesses
to the true nature of the deceased.

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:11.340
Sansuise
Second
Judgement
Offices of Shoko
Koshinen
First Judgement
Offices of Shinko
Yukyoto

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:01.870
The Offices of Shoko observe the Sanzu River,

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:05.920
making sure the dead cross where
they are supposed to and don't pull any tricks.

00:17:06.210 --> 00:17:10.420
Plus, they thoroughly investigate any killing
or theft the dead were responsible for.

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:16.090
When you hear "killing,"
you might being thinking "homicide,"

00:17:16.090 --> 00:17:20.220
but the overwhelming majority of offenses
actually take place against animals.

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:27.150
And that is why, when it comes to the role
of material witness, each of these pets is brought along.

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:30.690
Do people nowadays all have pets?

00:17:31.530 --> 00:17:33.820
Naturally, there are some people who don't,

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:39.320
so we receive testimony from killifish and tadpoles
and such that were present in their classrooms.

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:43.000
That means every single unruly boy's in a real jam!

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:47.330
Which is why one must treat living things with care.

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:54.760
Speaking about the accused, your pet cat Mikke says
that every day for several hours you'd go on saying,

00:17:54.880 --> 00:18:00.390
"There, there. What's the matter? Is it food you want,
Mikke?" and that you were a good, affectionate owner.

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:03.520
Are you praising me or belittling me?! Which is it?!

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:07.140
When he's in front of me, this guy cries purrty often.

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:10.110
Mikke...! That's enough already!

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:15.190
In cases like this where the guy's embarrassed
about how affectionate he was,

00:18:15.190 --> 00:18:16.860
I'd say it's actually torture.

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:21.700
Well, in recent years it seems
such people have been relatively numerous.

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:24.120
Witnesses, please come forward!

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:26.250
EEEK! Huh? All of them?! I'm sorry, okay?!

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:30.170
You can really tell he's the kind of guy
who romped around during summer vacation!
EEEK! Huh? All of them?! I'm sorry, okay?!

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:32.130
I see...

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:36.470
People's behavior toward animals is an area where
aspects of their true character become readily apparent.

00:18:37.010 --> 00:18:42.300
Of course, not everything is determined by this alone,
but it's a large point of reference.

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:47.600
Whether one loves or hates animals
also becomes a vital point of reference.

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:53.400
People who like animals and therefore
make contact with them in good faith.

00:18:53.940 --> 00:18:57.690
People who, even if they like animals,
dote on them in a self-centered kind of way.

00:18:57.690 --> 00:19:02.070
Those who don't like animals, but who still
find a way to pay attention to their needs.

00:19:02.410 --> 00:19:05.040
Those you don't like animals
and choose to tyrannize them.

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:07.410
You can really see people's dispositions.

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:07.330
Poison

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:12.580
Simply liking animals doesn't necessarily mean
one is a virtuous person.

00:19:13.090 --> 00:19:17.670
That's right! After all, some people who put their pets first
are big pains in the butt nevertheless.

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:20.260
And there are some fidgety dogs out there, too!

00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:24.970
Which is why I kept a tight leash on you
when we went to the Mundane World.

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:26.810
Yep.

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:28.060
An excellent decision.

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:31.770
The theory that certain aspects of one's character
readily come out when they deal with animals,

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:34.270
is most easily understood by watching Mr. Hozuki.

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:38.360
Panda Chief of Staff, what is your name?

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:44.830
For the time being, people tentatively call me "Pan-kichi."

00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:47.490
Pan-kichi

00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:47.660
Until I got that name, I was simply called "Panda."

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:50.870
King Shoko's naming of things
is pretty half-hearted, huh?!

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:55.130
When people see me, each of them tends
to call me whatever name strikes their fancy.

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:58.000
For example, "Tonton" or "Pan-chan."

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:01.260
Well, when it comes to names,
something easy to understand is good.

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:04.050
King Shoko, do you truly have a love of animals?!

00:20:04.550 --> 00:20:10.100
He sure does. When he saw Kan from
the Offices of Sotai, he said, "Wow, how cute."

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:12.230
Kan

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:12.350
No one other than King Shoko
has said that up to this point.

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:20.740
Strange Yokai

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:16.400
Upon seeing a video
of that strange yokai Hakutaku drew,

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:20.610
King Shoko was once again the only one to say,
"What a lovely cat."

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:27.450
Strange Yokai
Total Views

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:24.990
What was Hakutaku thinking
when he posted that to a video-sharing site?

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:28.160
Nasubi might've been the one who posted it, you know.

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:28.120
Total Views

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:32.660
You're all companions of the famous Momotaro, right?

00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:35.250
If you like, why not work here?

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:35.960
Huh?

00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:52.430
Nah...

00:20:52.430 --> 00:20:53.140
Hm?

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:56.270
We work in Animal Cruelty Hell.

00:20:57.610 --> 00:21:01.820
Mr. Hozuki, you see, got mad at us
on Momotaro's behalf.

00:21:02.110 --> 00:21:06.110
So that's why we'll be working at Mr. Hozuki's place.

00:21:08.870 --> 00:21:10.910
Aha, I see.

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:14.330
Yeah, so we'll be heading home
and getting back to work now.

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:15.460
Yep.

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:25.510
Second Judgement:
Offices of Shoko

00:21:40.690 --> 00:21:42.570
Today, I'll treat you to a meal.

00:21:42.730 --> 00:21:43.440
What?!

00:21:43.440 --> 00:21:44.280
Really?!

00:21:44.820 --> 00:21:45.900
Alright, then meat, please!

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:46.990
Grapes!

00:21:46.990 --> 00:21:48.530
I'd sure like some mealworms.

00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:51.540
I'm so happy! Let's sing. One, two...

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:54.910
Everybody, clap your hands!
Blue demons, aren't they great?!

00:22:05.010 --> 00:22:10.760
Uso yo. Janakya naze koko ni tadoritsuku no?
That's a lie. If not, why do you find your way here?

00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:17.350
Enma-sama no mae de nao shira o kiru no ne
Even in front of Lord Enma, you feign ignorance

00:22:17.810 --> 00:22:23.280
Baka ne. Dakedo sonna toko tamaranakute
You're an idiot. But I can't get enough of that aspect of you

00:22:24.030 --> 00:22:29.660
Teitaraku. Onaji tsumi kasanetsuzuketa
What a predicament. You continued to repeat the same sin

00:22:30.320 --> 00:22:34.950
Ii no? Yubikiri genman.
Is that alright? Pinky swear.

00:22:34.950 --> 00:22:36.330
(E?)
(Huh?)
Ii no? Yubikiri genman.
Is that alright? Pinky swear.

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:41.170
Gachi ni honto ni naru yo.
It will seriously become reality.

00:22:41.170 --> 00:22:42.750
(Dogii!)
(Startling!)

00:22:41.170 --> 00:22:42.750
Gachi ni honto ni naru yo.
It will seriously become reality.

00:22:43.130 --> 00:22:49.130
Tensei o matazu shounetsu no mama ni
Without waiting for reincarnation, while still in the scorching heat

00:22:49.130 --> 00:22:55.180
Asa hiru eien ai o kushizashi narabete
Morning, midday, and eternally skewer desires and line them up

00:22:55.430 --> 00:22:58.350
Gutsu gutsu mou! Nie nie da yo
Already simmering! It's boiling

00:22:58.600 --> 00:23:01.770
Yuuge wa jigoku de hot pot
Supper is a hot pot in Hell

00:23:01.940 --> 00:23:07.990
Nita mono doushi ni oniai no oshioki
For people who are alike, a suitable punishment

00:23:08.150 --> 00:23:11.110
Juu juu achi! Koge koge da yo
Sizzling hot! It's burned to a crisp

00:23:11.320 --> 00:23:14.410
Anata to jigoku de hotcake
Hotcakes with you in Hell

00:23:14.580 --> 00:23:19.830
Tokoyo no suna ni naru made
Until they become forever-unchanging sand

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:26.800
NEXT TIME
ON HOZUKI'S

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:26.800
COOLHEADEDNESS...

00:23:26.050 --> 00:23:28.210
How are the Zashiki Warashi doing?

00:23:28.210 --> 00:23:29.130
They're doing well.

00:23:28.300 --> 00:23:28.880
AND

00:23:29.130 --> 00:23:31.300
Yesterday, I read a book to them again.

00:23:30.470 --> 00:23:31.090
BUT

00:23:31.300 --> 00:23:32.550
"Cinderella" or something?

00:23:32.550 --> 00:23:36.220
"The Lives of Marquis de Sade
and Leopold von Sacher-Masoch."

00:23:33.050 --> 00:23:33.970
SO

00:23:36.220 --> 00:23:38.980
Is Hell your intended destination?!

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:39.730
WE PRESENT:
UNRIVALED AT POKER

00:23:36.430 --> 00:23:39.730
AND
IS HELL YOUR
INTENDED DESTINATION?

00:23:36.430 --> 00:23:39.730
PLEASE ENJOY!
